{
 "id": "AT-RS-21, AT-RS-23, AT-RS-25, AT-RS-27, AT-RS-28, AT-RS-29, AT-RS-19 (helper part), AT-RS-24 (SESSION-RESTART §3.4, §3.5, §4.1, §5.2)",
 "note": "The terminal route's gate, arm, state change and claim against the launcher's file contract (protocol 1). A main Stop keeps the turn's permission mode, effort and transcript; PostCompact keeps no mode (its input has none on 2.1.312). D10: the newest read (the Stop's, or the mod's --seen-mode) when it is from the last turn (--turn-at: that turn's start, or the load's start with no turn in the load) or later, else (and with no --turn-at) the narrower of launch_mode (none: default) and that read, so an earlier process's Stop never widens a relaunch; plan against dontAsk and no read at all are mode-unknown. The gate: no launch folder (no-launcher); a relative, linked, wrongly named or not private folder, launcher.json missing or of another protocol or token, its pid not an ancestor of this claude (a fake process table) or another claude between them (nested), the folder bound to another session (launcher-invalid:<reason>); bypass the launch did not make available, a launch file gone, three relaunches in the hour (G3a); a transcript not named <sid>.jsonl; a release on hold or a hold that cannot be read (G5b); and the RS-P1 ship gate (fg-not-shipped) unless the test seam opens it. arm binds the folder (sid, O_EXCL) and writes the launch note (12 keys) and the carry note; set moves both, the launch note keeping its form; exiting and go need the ship gate (fg-not-shipped) and exiting the setting still on (off), with nothing written otherwise; claim takes the carry note only with restart.used holding its nonce and session, once. Arm checks again: the setting must still be on (off otherwise) and the terminal route needs the RS-P1 ship gate (fg-not-shipped), with nothing bound or written; a model that starts with - is note-pattern; Windows is unsupported-os. The sid file holds the session id and the binding claude's pid and start time: another session's arm or gate refuses other-session while that claude is another live process, and the arm rebinds the folder when it is this same claude (a /clear or /resume) or a gone one (before a relaunch); a file with no binder line is never taken over. Shadow: the launcher's checks do not refuse, and the reply says what G3 found",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
 "options": {"restart_on_update": "on"},
 "env": {"STORE_TEST_PROC": "$TMP/proc.txt", "STORE_TEST_CLAUDE_PID": "4242:Tue Oct 21 09:00:00 2026"},
 "steps": [
  {"setup": [
    {"write": "$TMP/proc.txt", "content": "4242 1 /opt/cc/claude/versions/2.1.311\n"},
    {"mkdir": "$TMP/rt", "mode": "0700"},
    {"mkdir": "$TMP/rt/L-0123456789abcdef", "mode": "0700"},
    {"write": "$TMP/rt/L-0123456789abcdef/launcher.json", "content": "{\"proto\":1,\"launcher_version\":\"0.1.2\",\"pid\":1,\"token\":\"0123456789abcdef\",\"started\":1792580000,\"cwd\":\"/w\",\"uname\":\"Darwin\",\"relaunches\":0,\"bypass_ok\":false,\"file_flags\":[\"$TMP/s.json\"],\"stamps\":\"stamps\"}\n"},
